// This source code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0
// © Ilai - Asset Divergence Detector (PCP / PSP) v5.9
// Pine Script V5
//
// v5.9 — the 5m/15m heads-up becomes an actual notice:
//  It was a cell in the breaks line, in parentheses, in the same small type as
//  everything beside it — so it read as one more entry in a list rather than
//  as something that just happened, and in practice it was never seen. It now
//  has a box of its own, with its own corner, its own text size and a tinted
//  background, and it is out of the breaks line entirely.
//    - PCP too, not only PSP. A PCP needs no swing, so it is known one bar
//      earlier than the PSP on the same candle; it shows grey with ◦ against
//      the coloured ⚡ of a PSP. It is much the more common of the two, hence
//      its own switch.
//    - A real alert() fires on a fast PSP, so TradingView can push it.
//  Still 138 series: f_fast gained the last closed bar's direction and paid
//  for it by packing its two swing booleans into one number (+2 high, +1 low,
//  so 3 is both).
//
// v5.8 — the daily divergence really was being missed, and this is why:
//  CME futures default to using the SETTLEMENT price as the daily close.
//  A chart can turn that off per symbol, and this one is turned off — but
//  request.security() knows nothing about a chart's per-symbol settings, so
//  it kept reading the settlement close while the bars on screen showed the
//  regular one. On a day that settles the other side of its open, the script
//  therefore read "up" for a candle the eye reads as down, no divergence
//  existed as far as it was concerned, and nothing was drawn. Swapping ES1!
//  for MES1! changed nothing because the default is the same on both.
//  Every symbol now goes through ticker.modify(settlement_as_close = ...)
//  before the request, defaulting to OFF so the script reads what the chart
//  draws. The debug rows print the open and close actually read, so the two
//  can be compared against the chart directly.
//
// v5.7:
//  - The chart timeframe's row in the panel reports nothing while the same
//    engine reports a live break on 1W, so the fault is somewhere on the
//    chart-timeframe path alone. Two guesses at it from reading the code
//    were both wrong, so the debug readout moves from the end of the line —
//    where it was pushed off a phone screen — into the panel, and prints the
//    raw values the engine is actually working from.
//  - The 5m/15m heads-up is parenthesised, "(5m ▲ ALL)". It was reading as
//    the same kind of thing as "1D ▲ NQ ES" when it is not: one is a
//    standing break, the other a moment. Brackets say "aside" without
//    adding a symbol to remember.
//
// v5.6 — fixes a desync v5.5 introduced:
//  v5.5 moved each timeframe's clock out of the request and onto the
//  built-in time_close(tf), to save a series. That is two different sources
//  updating independently: time_close() comes off the chart's own bar times,
//  the data comes off the request. The engine steps ONCE per timeframe bar,
//  on the clock — so if the clock advanced a bar before the data did, the
//  step ran on stale values and then did not run again until the next bar.
//  On a daily timeframe that leaves the state a day behind and yesterday's
//  divergence is never seen at all.
//  The clock goes back inside the tuple, where it advances in lockstep with
//  the data it times. To pay for it without returning to the memory limit,
//  close[1]/high[1]/low[1] collapse into the two values the "taken" test
//  actually compares, chosen inside the request. Still 138 series.
//  Also adds a debug switch that prints the directions the script actually
//  read, so a disagreement with the chart can be seen instead of guessed at.
//
// v5.5 — fixes "Memory limits exceeded", which v5.4 caused:
//  v5.4 added six more request.security calls, each returning an eleven
//  element tuple, taking the script from 144 stored series to 210. That is
//  the trap this file warns about below: it compiles clean and simply
//  refuses to load. The fix is to stop hauling raw numbers across and do
//  the work inside the request instead.
//    - The timeframe clock is now time_close(tf), a built-in that needs NO
//      request.security at all. One series saved per asset per timeframe.
//    - Candle direction is computed inside the request: one series instead
//      of the open and close it was derived from.
//    - The three-bar swing is computed inside the request: one boolean
//      instead of the three highs (or lows) it was derived from.
//    - The fast 5m/15m heads-up carries three series per asset instead of
//      eleven. It keeps no state and tests no levels, so it needs neither
//      the levels nor the clock.
//  Result: 138 stored series, below the 144 that loaded fine before v5.4.
//
// v5.4:
//  - The CHART'S OWN timeframe is back in the line. Leaving it out was a
//    mistake: an undecided PCP shows on the bars only as a tiny grey dot and
//    a PCP that never became a swing shows nothing at all, so on a daily
//    chart the daily state was invisible everywhere. It costs no extra
//    request.security — it is built from the chart series already fetched,
//    so there is no sampling problem either.
//  - Fast heads-up for 5m and 15m, in the SAME line rather than a second row.
//    It does NOT go through the carried-state engine; it is computed directly
//    on the last bar, which is exactly what lets it read a timeframe below the
//    chart's without the once-per-chart-bar sampling ruining it. It stands
//    until the next close on its own timeframe, and skips the chart's own
//    timeframe, which is already drawn on the bars.
//
// v5.3:
//  - The line lists EVERY standing break from 1H / 4H / 1D / 1W side by
//    side again, not just the most recent one. The timeframe gate is
//    unchanged: on a 1H chart 1H is absent, because it is drawn on the bars.
//  - Each timeframe owns one cell with three states — a standing break in
//    its direction's colour, else the grey pending bar, else nothing.
//  - "live" is now a flag of its own instead of dir == 0, so dir and who
//    survive an invalidation and the "broken" alert can still name what broke.
//
// v5.2:
//  - The markers on the bars use the small triangles ▴ ▾ / ▵ ▿ instead of the
//    full-height ▲ ▼ / △ ▽. Same family, about half the height, and the
//    solid-vs-hollow distinction survives intact. size.tiny is kept on
//    purpose: size.auto would shrink them to nothing when zoomed out.
//
// v5.1 — the line says what happened and who was in it, nothing else:
//  - A record is "<TF> <arrow> <who>". "who" is the assets that took part in
//    the DIVERGENCE, or "ALL" when all three did. The P/Y/B source letter is
//    gone: the list of names already says where the divergence came from.
//  - No timestamp. The line reports that a break happened, not when.
//  - No timer and no "broken" text. A break whose level is taken simply
//    disappears.
//  - Grey state: a higher-timeframe bar that closed as a PCP
//    but whose swing verdict is not in yet. Same idea as the grey dot on the
//    bars, and it clears itself the same way — the next close either promotes
//    it to a coloured break or drops it.
//
// v5.0:
//  - ONE slot instead of one record per timeframe.
//
// v4.x history:
//  - YM only creates a divergence when it shows STRENGTH (up while ES and/or
//    NQ are down). ES vs NQ: any direction mismatch counts.
//  - Swing detected on EVERY included asset: solid ▴/▾ when the swing is on
//    the chart symbol, hollow ▵/▿ when it is on another asset only.
//  - Pending marker (•) while a PCP bar's swing verdict is not in yet.
//  - Weekly is a full category, on the chart and in the line.
//  - Symbols are three input.symbol fields, so only three contracts load.

//@version=5
indicator("Asset Divergence | PCP & PSP v5", shorttitle="ADI v5",
     overlay       = true,
     max_bars_back = 5000)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  INPUTS
//  Hebrew labels. Every option string below is also compared in code —
//  translating one without the other silently breaks the setting.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

grp_mode   = "═══  זיהוי  ═══"
i_ignore_doji = input.bool(false, title="התעלם מדוג'י (סגירה = פתיחה)",
     tooltip="כבוי (ברירת מחדל): דוג'י נחשב כיוון שונה ויכול ליצור PCP.\nדלוק: דוג'י ניטרלי ולעולם לא יוצר PCP.",
     group=grp_mode)

grp_assets = "═══  נכסים  ═══"
i_sym_nq   = input.symbol("NQ1!", title="סימבול NQ", group=grp_assets,
     tooltip="למעבר למיקרו — החלף את שלושת השדות ל-MNQ1! / MES1! / MYM1!\nחשוב לשמור על שלושתם מאותה משפחת חוזים; ערבוב גדלי טיק מעוות את ההשוואה.")
i_sym_es   = input.symbol("ES1!", title="סימבול ES", group=grp_assets)
i_sym_ym   = input.symbol("YM1!", title="סימבול YM", group=grp_assets)
i_use_nq   = input.bool(true,  title="כלול NQ", group=grp_assets)
i_use_es   = input.bool(true,  title="כלול ES", group=grp_assets)
i_use_ym   = input.bool(true,  title="כלול YM (חוזקה בלבד)",
     tooltip="YM יוצר דיברגנס רק כשהוא נסגר בעלייה בזמן ש-ES ו/או NQ נסגרים בירידה.",
     group=grp_assets)
i_settle   = input.string("כבוי — כמו הגרף", title="Settlement כסגירה יומית",
     options=["כבוי — כמו הגרף", "דלוק", "ברירת המחדל של הסימבול"],
     tooltip="בחוזי CME ברירת המחדל היא שהסגירה היומית היא מחיר הסילוק, לא הסגירה הרגילה.\nהגדרת הגרף שלך לא עוברת ל-request.security, ולכן בלי זה הסקריפט קורא נר אחר ממה שאתה רואה.\nהשאר על 'כבוי' אם ההגדרה בגרף לא מסומנת.",
     group=grp_assets)

grp_tf     = "═══  מסגרת הגרף  ═══"
i_tf_1m    = input.bool(true,  title="1m (ES ו-NQ בלבד)", group=grp_tf)
i_tf_5m    = input.bool(true,  title="5m",     group=grp_tf)
i_tf_15m   = input.bool(true,  title="15m",    group=grp_tf)
i_tf_1h    = input.bool(true,  title="1H",     group=grp_tf)
i_tf_4h    = input.bool(true,  title="4H",     group=grp_tf)
i_tf_1d    = input.bool(true,  title="יומי",   group=grp_tf)
i_tf_1w    = input.bool(true,  title="שבועי",  group=grp_tf)

grp_col    = "═══  סימונים וצבעים  ═══"
i_col_bull = input.color(color.new(#00e5ff, 0), title="אות שורי", group=grp_col)
i_col_bear = input.color(color.new(#ff1744, 0), title="אות דובי", group=grp_col)
i_ext_transp = input.int(45, title="עמעום סימון של נכס אחר", minval=0, maxval=90,
     tooltip="שקיפות הסימון החלול, שמצויר כשהסווינג קרה בנכס אחר ולא בסימבול שעל הגרף.",
     group=grp_col)
i_show_pending = input.bool(true, title="הצג סימון PCP ממתין (•)",
     tooltip="נר PCP מוכרע רק כשהנר שאחריו נסגר. עד אז הוא מסומן בנקודה עמומה.",
     group=grp_col)
i_col_pend = input.color(color.new(#9e9e9e, 25), title="צבע PCP ממתין", group=grp_col)
i_show_pcp_bars = input.bool(false, title="צבע את כל נרות ה-PCP", group=grp_col)
i_col_pcp  = input.color(color.new(#ffd54f, 80), title="גוון נרות PCP", group=grp_col)

grp_mtf    = "═══  מסגרות זמן גבוהות  ═══"
i_mtf_on   = input.bool(true, title="הצג שורת שבירות",
     tooltip="שורה אחת בפינה: השבירה האחרונה מ-1H / 4H / 1D / 1W, ולידה באפור נר שנסגר עם דיברגנס וממתין להכרעה אם הוא סווינג.\nשבירה חדשה מחליפה את הקודמת. מוצגות רק מסגרות גבוהות ממסגרת הגרף.",
     group=grp_mtf)
i_mtf_v    = input.string("למטה", title="גובה השורה",
     options=["למעלה", "באמצע", "למטה"], group=grp_mtf)
i_mtf_h    = input.string("שמאל", title="צד השורה",
     options=["שמאל", "מרכז", "ימין"], group=grp_mtf)
i_mtf_pad  = input.int(0, title="הרחקת השורה מהקצה (שורות)", minval=0, maxval=12,
     tooltip="מוסיף שורות ריקות בין השורה לקצה הגרף, כדי להרים אותה מעל שורה של אינדיקטור אחר שיושב באותה פינה.",
     group=grp_mtf)
i_inv_wick = input.bool(false, title="בטל שבירה לפי פתיל",
     tooltip="כבוי (ברירת מחדל): שבירה מתה כשנר של אותה מסגרת נסגר מעבר לרמת הסווינג.\nדלוק: מספיק פתיל מעבר לרמה.",
     group=grp_mtf)
i_pnl_on   = input.bool(false, title="הצג פאנל מסגרות",
     tooltip="תצוגה מלאה: שורה לכל מסגרת עם השבירה החיה שלה. משלימה את השורה, שמראה רק את האחרונה.",
     group=grp_mtf)
i_pnl_v    = input.string("למטה", title="גובה הפאנל",
     options=["למעלה", "באמצע", "למטה"], group=grp_mtf)
i_pnl_h    = input.string("ימין", title="צד הפאנל",
     options=["שמאל", "מרכז", "ימין"], group=grp_mtf)
i_pnl_pad  = input.int(0, title="הרחקת הפאנל מהקצה (שורות)", minval=0, maxval=12, group=grp_mtf)
i_col_neut = input.color(color.new(#ffffff, 15), title="צבע טקסט נייטרלי", group=grp_mtf)
i_mtf_alert = input.bool(true, title="התראה על שבירה חדשה ועל ביטול", group=grp_mtf)
i_debug    = input.bool(false, title="הצג ערכי בדיקה (בפאנל)",
     tooltip="מוסיף לפאנל ארבע שורות עם הערכים הגולמיים של מסגרת הגרף:\nd1 = כיוון הנר האחרון שנסגר · d2 = הנר שלפניו · sw = סווינגים · st = מצב המנוע.\nצריך להדליק גם את הפאנל.",
     group=grp_mtf)

grp_fast   = "═══  התרעה מהירה 5m / 15m  ═══"
i_fast_on  = input.bool(true, title="הצג התרעת 5m / 15m",
     tooltip="תיבה נפרדת משלה, לא שורת השבירות. מופיעה בכל גרף חוץ ממסגרת ההתרעה עצמה — 5 דקות לא תוצג על גרף 5 דקות, 15 דקות לא על גרף 15 דקות.\nנעלמת מעצמה בסגירת הנר הבא של אותה מסגרת.",
     group=grp_fast)
i_fast_pcp = input.bool(true, title="כלול גם PCP (דיברגנס בלי סווינג)",
     tooltip="PSP מוצג בצבע עם ⚡. PCP מוצג באפור עם ◦, ומופיע נר אחד מוקדם יותר כי הוא לא מחכה לסווינג.\nPCP הרבה יותר שכיח — כבה את זה אם זה מרעיש.",
     group=grp_fast)
i_fast_v   = input.string("למעלה", title="גובה ההתרעה",
     options=["למעלה", "באמצע", "למטה"], group=grp_fast)
i_fast_h   = input.string("מרכז", title="צד ההתרעה",
     options=["שמאל", "מרכז", "ימין"], group=grp_fast)
i_fast_pad = input.int(0, title="הרחקת ההתרעה מהקצה (שורות)", minval=0, maxval=12, group=grp_fast)
i_fast_sz  = input.string("גדול", title="גודל הטקסט",
     options=["קטן", "רגיל", "גדול", "ענק"], group=grp_fast)
i_fast_bg  = input.bool(true, title="רקע מודגש", group=grp_fast)
i_fast_alert = input.bool(true, title="התראה (alert) על PSP מהיר",
     tooltip="שולח alert של TradingView כשנוצר PSP מהיר, כדי שאפשר יהיה לקבל התראה לנייד.\nלכל היותר אחת לנר של הגרף — על גרף שעתי זו אחת לשעה.",
     group=grp_fast)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  TIMEFRAME GATE  (chart drawing only — the corner line is independent)
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

tf_str = timeframe.period

is_1m  = tf_str == "1"
is_5m  = tf_str == "5"
is_15m = tf_str == "15"
is_1h  = tf_str == "60"
is_4h  = tf_str == "240"
is_1d  = tf_str == "D"
is_1w  = tf_str == "W"

tf_allowed = (is_1m  and i_tf_1m)  or
             (is_5m  and i_tf_5m)  or
             (is_15m and i_tf_15m) or
             (is_1h  and i_tf_1h)  or
             (is_4h  and i_tf_4h)  or
             (is_1d  and i_tf_1d)  or
             (is_1w  and i_tf_1w)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  CANDLE DIRECTION  (+1 Bull / -1 Bear / 0 Doji)
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

f_dir(float o, float c) =>
    c > o ? 1 : c < o ? -1 : 0

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  CHART-TIMEFRAME FETCHES
//  lookahead_off → proper backtest support for all timeframes
//  gaps_off      → no na bars when the external symbol has no tick
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

settleMode = i_settle == "דלוק" ? settlement_as_close.on : i_settle == "ברירת המחדל של הסימבול" ? settlement_as_close.inherit : settlement_as_close.off

tk_nq = ticker.modify(i_sym_nq, settlement_as_close = settleMode)
tk_es = ticker.modify(i_sym_es, settlement_as_close = settleMode)
tk_ym = ticker.modify(i_sym_ym, settlement_as_close = settleMode)

f_sec(simple string sym) =>
    [o, h, l, c] = request.security(sym, timeframe.period,
         [open, high, low, close],
         lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off,
         gaps      = barmerge.gaps_off)
    [o, h, l, c]

[a_nq_o, a_nq_h, a_nq_l, a_nq_c] = f_sec(tk_nq)
[a_es_o, a_es_h, a_es_l, a_es_c] = f_sec(tk_es)
[a_ym_o, a_ym_h, a_ym_l, a_ym_c] = f_sec(tk_ym)

nq_dir = f_dir(a_nq_o, a_nq_c)
es_dir = f_dir(a_es_o, a_es_c)
ym_dir = f_dir(a_ym_o, a_ym_c)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PCP DETECTION
//
//  ES vs NQ : any direction mismatch is a divergence.
//  YM       : asymmetric — YM only matters when it shows STRENGTH,
//             i.e. YM closes UP while ES and/or NQ close DOWN.
//             YM down against the other two up is NOT a signal.
//  1m       : YM is excluded entirely.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

nq_ok = i_use_nq and (not i_ignore_doji or nq_dir != 0)
es_ok = i_use_es and (not i_ignore_doji or es_dir != 0)
ym_ok = i_use_ym and not is_1m and (not i_ignore_doji or ym_dir != 0)

div_es_nq = nq_ok and es_ok and (nq_dir != es_dir)

div_ym = ym_ok and ym_dir > 0 and
         ((es_ok and es_dir < 0) or (nq_ok and nq_dir < 0))

is_pcp = div_es_nq or div_ym

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PSP DETECTION  — 3-Bar Swing, Zero Repaint, No Flicker
//
//  Timeline:   bar[2] ←  bar[1]  ← bar[0]
//                       (SWING)    (confirms, current CLOSED bar)
//
//  The swing is checked on EVERY included asset, not only on the chart
//  symbol, so a swing that happens on NQ while the chart shows ES is
//  still marked — just with a hollow marker so it is never confused
//  with a swing on the bars in front of you.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

f_sw_hi(float h) => h[1] > h[2] and h[1] > h[0]
f_sw_lo(float l) => l[1] < l[2] and l[1] < l[0]

own_hi = f_sw_hi(high)
own_lo = f_sw_lo(low)

ext_hi = (i_use_nq  and f_sw_hi(a_nq_h)) or
         (i_use_es  and f_sw_hi(a_es_h)) or
         (div_ym[1] and f_sw_hi(a_ym_h))

ext_lo = (i_use_nq  and f_sw_lo(a_nq_l)) or
         (i_use_es  and f_sw_lo(a_es_l)) or
         (div_ym[1] and f_sw_lo(a_ym_l))

confirmed = barstate.isconfirmed
pcp_at_1  = is_pcp[1]          // immutable — bar[1] is fully closed

psp_base     = tf_allowed and confirmed and pcp_at_1

psp_bear_own = psp_base and own_hi
psp_bear_ext = psp_base and ext_hi and not own_hi
psp_bull_own = psp_base and own_lo
psp_bull_ext = psp_base and ext_lo and not own_lo

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PSP MARKERS
//  offset = -1 places the marker on bar[1] — the bar that was resolved.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

c_bear_ext = color.new(i_col_bear, i_ext_transp)
c_bull_ext = color.new(i_col_bull, i_ext_transp)

plotchar(psp_bear_own ? 1 : na, title="PSP Bear — Own Asset",
     char="▴", location=location.abovebar, color=i_col_bear,
     offset=-1, size=size.tiny)

plotchar(psp_bear_ext ? 1 : na, title="PSP Bear — Other Asset",
     char="▵", location=location.abovebar, color=c_bear_ext,
     offset=-1, size=size.tiny)

plotchar(psp_bull_own ? 1 : na, title="PSP Bull — Own Asset",
     char="▾", location=location.belowbar, color=i_col_bull,
     offset=-1, size=size.tiny)

plotchar(psp_bull_ext ? 1 : na, title="PSP Bull — Other Asset",
     char="▿", location=location.belowbar, color=c_bull_ext,
     offset=-1, size=size.tiny)

// ── Pending: self-clearing, because a bar is undecided exactly while
//    barstate.isconfirmed is false. Historical bars are always confirmed.
pending = tf_allowed and i_show_pending and not confirmed

plotchar(pending and is_pcp    ? 1 : na, title="PCP Pending — Live Bar",
     char="•", location=location.abovebar, color=i_col_pend, size=size.tiny)

plotchar(pending and is_pcp[1] ? 1 : na, title="PCP Pending — Previous Bar",
     char="•", location=location.abovebar, color=i_col_pend,
     offset=-1, size=size.tiny)

barcolor(tf_allowed and i_show_pcp_bars and is_pcp ? i_col_pcp : na,
     title="PCP Bar Tint")

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  HIGHER TIMEFRAMES
//
//  request.security returns RAW NUMBERS only — never a UDT and never an
//  array. Returning an object would make TradingView keep a copy per chart
//  bar per timeframe and blow the memory limit ("Memory limits exceeded",
//  which compiles cleanly and simply fails to load).
//
//  Every history offset is taken INSIDE the expression, so it is evaluated
//  in that timeframe's own context and a bar only enters the calculation
//  once it has closed. Zero repaint.
//
//  Index map in the requested timeframe's context:
//      [1] = last CLOSED bar   confirms the swing of [2], carries the close
//                              used for the "level taken" test, and is itself
//                              the bar the grey pending state is read from
//      [2] = the SWING bar
//      [3] = the bar before it
//
//  The call count is fixed in the source (4 timeframes × 3 assets = 12,
//  plus 3 for the chart timeframe) and never varies with the chart.
//
//  Limitation worth knowing: the state is built by stepping through the chart's
//  own history, so a timeframe can only be tracked as far back as the chart
//  reaches. A 1m chart holds days, not weeks, so 1W will rarely fire there.
//  Watch the weekly and daily from a 15m chart or higher.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// What a stepped timeframe needs, and nothing more. d1/d2 are directions
// already reduced inside the request; swH/swL are the three-bar swing already
// decided there. hi2/lo2 are the swing bar's extremes, which become the level
// to defend. tkH/tkL are the bar that just closed, already reduced to the
// one value each side of the "taken" test needs.
type AB
    float d1  = na
    float d2  = na
    bool  swH = false
    bool  swL = false
    float hi2 = na
    float lo2 = na
    float tkH = na
    float tkL = na

// The fast heads-up keeps no state and tests no level. It needs the last
// closed bar's direction (that alone decides a PCP), the swing bar's direction
// and the swing itself — and the two swing booleans are packed into ONE number
// (+2 for a swing high, +1 for a swing low, so 3 means both) because every
// element of every request is a full series held over the chart's history.
type FB
    float d1 = na
    float d2 = na
    float sw = na

//  The clock rides INSIDE the tuple on purpose. Timing it from the built-in
//  time_close(tf) instead desynchronises it from the data it is timing: the
//  engine steps once per bar on the clock, so a clock that moves first makes
//  that one step read stale values, and the state then sits wrong until the
//  next bar. Here they can only move together.
f_load(AB b, simple string sym, simple string tf) =>
    [tc, d1, d2, swH, swL, hi2, lo2, tkH, tkL] = request.security(sym, tf,
         [time_close[1],
          close[1] > open[1] ? 1.0 : close[1] < open[1] ? -1.0 : na(close[1]) ? na : 0.0,
          close[2] > open[2] ? 1.0 : close[2] < open[2] ? -1.0 : na(close[2]) ? na : 0.0,
          high[2] > high[3] and high[2] > high[1],
          low[2]  < low[3]  and low[2]  < low[1],
          high[2], low[2],
          i_inv_wick ? high[1] : close[1],
          i_inv_wick ? low[1]  : close[1]],
         lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off,
         gaps      = barmerge.gaps_off)
    b.d1  := d1
    b.d2  := d2
    b.swH := swH
    b.swL := swL
    b.hi2 := hi2
    b.lo2 := lo2
    b.tkH := tkH
    b.tkL := tkL
    tc

f_fast(FB b, simple string sym, simple string tf) =>
    [d1, d2, sw] = request.security(sym, tf,
         [close[1] > open[1] ? 1.0 : close[1] < open[1] ? -1.0 : na(close[1]) ? na : 0.0,
          close[2] > open[2] ? 1.0 : close[2] < open[2] ? -1.0 : na(close[2]) ? na : 0.0,
          (high[2] > high[3] and high[2] > high[1] ? 2.0 : 0.0) + (low[2] < low[3] and low[2] < low[1] ? 1.0 : 0.0)],
         lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off,
         gaps      = barmerge.gaps_off)
    b.d1 := d1
    b.d2 := d2
    b.sw := sw
    b.d2

// The chart's own timeframe needs no request.security at all — its series are
// already here. [1] is the last closed bar, matching the index map above.
f_fill(AB b, float o, float h, float l, float c) =>
    b.d1  := c[1] > o[1] ? 1.0 : c[1] < o[1] ? -1.0 : na(c[1]) ? na : 0.0
    b.d2  := c[2] > o[2] ? 1.0 : c[2] < o[2] ? -1.0 : na(c[2]) ? na : 0.0
    b.swH := h[2] > h[3] and h[2] > h[1]
    b.swL := l[2] < l[3] and l[2] < l[1]
    b.hi2 := h[2]
    b.lo2 := l[2]
    b.tkH := i_inv_wick ? h[1] : c[1]
    b.tkL := i_inv_wick ? l[1] : c[1]
    b.tkL

// One reusable object per asset per timeframe — allocated once, updated in
// place, so nothing accumulates across bars.
var AB n1h = AB.new()
var AB e1h = AB.new()
var AB y1h = AB.new()
var AB n4h = AB.new()
var AB e4h = AB.new()
var AB y4h = AB.new()
var AB n1d = AB.new()
var AB e1d = AB.new()
var AB y1d = AB.new()
var AB n1w = AB.new()
var AB e1w = AB.new()
var AB y1w = AB.new()
var AB nCh = AB.new()
var AB eCh = AB.new()
var AB yCh = AB.new()
var FB n15 = FB.new()
var FB e15 = FB.new()
var FB y15 = FB.new()
var FB n5m = FB.new()
var FB e5m = FB.new()
var FB y5m = FB.new()

tn1h = f_load(n1h, tk_nq, "60")
te1h = f_load(e1h, tk_es, "60")
ty1h = f_load(y1h, tk_ym, "60")

tn4h = f_load(n4h, tk_nq, "240")
te4h = f_load(e4h, tk_es, "240")
ty4h = f_load(y4h, tk_ym, "240")

tn1d = f_load(n1d, tk_nq, "D")
te1d = f_load(e1d, tk_es, "D")
ty1d = f_load(y1d, tk_ym, "D")

tn1w = f_load(n1w, tk_nq, "W")
te1w = f_load(e1w, tk_es, "W")
ty1w = f_load(y1w, tk_ym, "W")

// The two fast timeframes. Read on the last bar only, never stepped through
// history, so a chart above them is not a problem.
f_fast(n15, tk_nq, "15")
f_fast(e15, tk_es, "15")
f_fast(y15, tk_ym, "15")

f_fast(n5m, tk_nq, "5")
f_fast(e5m, tk_es, "5")
f_fast(y5m, tk_ym, "5")

f_fill(nCh, a_nq_o, a_nq_h, a_nq_l, a_nq_c)
f_fill(eCh, a_es_o, a_es_h, a_es_l, a_es_c)
f_fill(yCh, a_ym_o, a_ym_h, a_ym_l, a_ym_c)

// The clock each engine steps on, taken from whichever asset is enabled.
// It came across in the same tuple as the data, so the two cannot drift.
t1h = i_use_nq ? tn1h : i_use_es ? te1h : ty1h
t4h = i_use_nq ? tn4h : i_use_es ? te4h : ty4h
t1d = i_use_nq ? tn1d : i_use_es ? te1d : ty1d
t1w = i_use_nq ? tn1w : i_use_es ? te1w : ty1w

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PER-TIMEFRAME STATE
//  Lives in var on the CHART's timeline, which is where state belongs.
//  The rule against objects applies to what request.security returns.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

type MtfSt
    int    lastT  = 0     // time of the bar already stepped — blocks a double step
    bool   live   = false // a break is standing right now
    int    dir    = 0     // -1 bearish · 1 bullish — kept after an invalidation
    string who    = ""    // assets that took part in the divergence, or "ALL"
    bool   isNew  = false // set on the chart bar the break was recorded
    bool   isGone = false // set on the chart bar it was invalidated
    bool   pndOn  = false // the bar that just closed is a PCP, verdict not in
    string pndWho = ""

// Has the level been taken? tkH and tkL are already the right side to compare
// — the request picked close or wick according to i_inv_wick.
f_taken(float lvl, int dir, float tkH, float tkL) =>
    na(lvl) ? false : dir == -1 ? tkH > lvl : tkL < lvl

// Who took part in the divergence. ES and NQ are both in whenever they split;
// YM is in only when its strength rule fired, and it drags in whichever of the
// other two it was strong against.
f_who(bool divP, bool divY, bool okN, bool okE, int dn, int de) =>
    pN = divP or (divY and okN and dn < 0)
    pE = divP or (divY and okE and de < 0)
    w  = pN and pE and divY ? "ALL" : ""
    if w == ""
        if pN
            w := "NQ"
        if pE
            w := w + (w == "" ? "" : " ") + "ES"
        if divY
            w := w + (w == "" ? "" : " ") + "YM"
    w

// Levels of the assets that made the swing, kept out of the type so the state
// stays about the break and these stay about the price test.
type Lv
    float nq = na
    float es = na
    float ym = na

var Lv v1h = Lv.new()
var Lv v4h = Lv.new()
var Lv v1d = Lv.new()
var Lv v1w = Lv.new()

// One step per closed bar of that timeframe. Invalidation is checked before
// detection, so a level taken and a fresh swing on the same bar resolve in
// the right order.
f_step(MtfSt s, Lv v, int t, AB n, AB e, AB y) =>
    s.isNew  := false
    s.isGone := false
    if not na(t) and t != s.lastT
        s.lastT := t

        // ── 1. was the level taken by the bar that just closed? ──
        if s.live
            tkN = f_taken(v.nq, s.dir, n.tkH, n.tkL)
            tkE = f_taken(v.es, s.dir, e.tkH, e.tkL)
            tkY = f_taken(v.ym, s.dir, y.tkH, y.tkL)
            if tkN or tkE or tkY
                s.live   := false
                s.isGone := true
                v.nq := na
                v.es := na
                v.ym := na

        // ── 2. the bar that just closed, [1]: a PCP whose swing verdict
        //       needs the NEXT close. This is the grey "maybe" state, and it
        //       is replaced wholesale on the next step, so it self-clears.
        qN  = i_use_nq and not na(n.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or n.d1 != 0)
        qE  = i_use_es and not na(e.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or e.d1 != 0)
        qY  = i_use_ym and not na(y.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or y.d1 != 0)
        qP  = qN and qE and n.d1 != e.d1
        qYm = qY and y.d1 > 0 and ((qE and e.d1 < 0) or (qN and n.d1 < 0))
        s.pndOn  := qP or qYm
        s.pndWho := s.pndOn ? f_who(qP, qYm, qN, qE, int(n.d1), int(e.d1)) : ""

        // ── 3. a new PSP on the swing bar, [2] ──
        okN = i_use_nq and not na(n.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or n.d2 != 0)
        okE = i_use_es and not na(e.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or e.d2 != 0)
        okY = i_use_ym and not na(y.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or y.d2 != 0)

        divP = okN and okE and n.d2 != e.d2
        divY = okY and y.d2 > 0 and ((okE and e.d2 < 0) or (okN and n.d2 < 0))

        if divP or divY
            hiN = i_use_nq and n.swH
            hiE = i_use_es and e.swH
            hiY = divY     and y.swH
            loN = i_use_nq and n.swL
            loE = i_use_es and e.swL
            loY = divY     and y.swL

            nHi = (hiN ? 1 : 0) + (hiE ? 1 : 0) + (hiY ? 1 : 0)
            nLo = (loN ? 1 : 0) + (loE ? 1 : 0) + (loY ? 1 : 0)

            if nHi > 0 or nLo > 0
                bear = nHi >= nLo          // tie goes to the swing high
                gN   = bear ? hiN : loN
                gE   = bear ? hiE : loE
                gY   = bear ? hiY : loY

                s.live   := true
                s.dir    := bear ? -1 : 1
                s.who    := f_who(divP, divY, okN, okE, int(n.d2), int(e.d2))
                s.isNew  := true
                s.isGone := false
                v.nq := gN ? (bear ? n.hi2 : n.lo2) : na
                v.es := gE ? (bear ? e.hi2 : e.lo2) : na
                v.ym := gY ? (bear ? y.hi2 : y.lo2) : na
    s.live

var MtfSt st1h = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt st4h = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt st1d = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt st1w = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt stCh = MtfSt.new()
var Lv    vCh  = Lv.new()

f_step(stCh, vCh, time, nCh, eCh, yCh)
f_step(st1h, v1h, t1h, n1h, e1h, y1h)
f_step(st4h, v4h, t4h, n4h, e4h, y4h)
f_step(st1d, v1d, t1d, n1d, e1d, y1d)
f_step(st1w, v1w, t1w, n1w, e1w, y1w)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE LINE
//
//  Order:  1W · 1D · 4H · 1H · [your chart] · 15m · 5m
//
//  Each cell renders one of three states: a standing break in its
//  direction's colour, otherwise the grey bar that closed with a divergence
//  and is still waiting on its swing verdict, otherwise nothing. Cells pack
//  left, so gaps close up.
//
//  A timeframe between the chart's and the fast pair is left out: stepping
//  it through history would sample it once per chart bar and the carried
//  "level taken" state would come out wrong. The chart's own timeframe has
//  no such problem — it is built from the chart's own series.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
sh1h = timeframe.in_seconds("60")  > chartSec
sh4h = timeframe.in_seconds("240") > chartSec
sh1d = timeframe.in_seconds("D")   > chartSec
sh1w = timeframe.in_seconds("W")   > chartSec

chName = is_1m ? "1m" : is_5m ? "5m" : is_15m ? "15m" : is_1h ? "1H" : is_4h ? "4H" : is_1d ? "1D" : is_1w ? "1W" : tf_str

f_arrow(MtfSt s) =>
    s.dir < 0 ? "▼" : "▲"

f_rec(MtfSt s, string nm) =>
    s.live ? nm + " " + f_arrow(s) + " " + s.who : i_show_pending and s.pndOn ? nm + " ◦ " + s.pndWho : ""

f_col(MtfSt s) =>
    s.live ? (s.dir < 0 ? i_col_bear : i_col_bull) : i_col_pend

r1w = sh1w ? f_rec(st1w, "1W") : ""
r1d = sh1d ? f_rec(st1d, "1D") : ""
r4h = sh4h ? f_rec(st4h, "4H") : ""
r1h = sh1h ? f_rec(st1h, "1H") : ""
rCh = tf_allowed ? f_rec(stCh, chName) : ""

// ── the fast heads-up ──
//  Deliberately NOT the carried-state engine. A PSP is a function of three
//  bars, so it can be read straight off the last bar, and that is what lets
//  this work on a timeframe below the chart's: nothing is accumulated across
//  history, so nothing can be corrupted by sampling it once per chart bar.
f_swH(float sw) =>
    not na(sw) and sw >= 2.0

f_swL(float sw) =>
    not na(sw) and (sw == 1.0 or sw == 3.0)

f_flash(FB n, FB e, FB y) =>
    // ── PSP: the swing bar [2], confirmed by the bar that just closed ──
    okN = i_use_nq and not na(n.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or n.d2 != 0)
    okE = i_use_es and not na(e.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or e.d2 != 0)
    okY = i_use_ym and not na(y.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or y.d2 != 0)

    divP = okN and okE and n.d2 != e.d2
    divY = okY and y.d2 > 0 and ((okE and e.d2 < 0) or (okN and n.d2 < 0))

    on  = false
    dir = 0
    who = ""
    if divP or divY
        hiN = i_use_nq and f_swH(n.sw)
        hiE = i_use_es and f_swH(e.sw)
        hiY = divY     and f_swH(y.sw)
        loN = i_use_nq and f_swL(n.sw)
        loE = i_use_es and f_swL(e.sw)
        loY = divY     and f_swL(y.sw)

        nHi = (hiN ? 1 : 0) + (hiE ? 1 : 0) + (hiY ? 1 : 0)
        nLo = (loN ? 1 : 0) + (loE ? 1 : 0) + (loY ? 1 : 0)

        if nHi > 0 or nLo > 0
            on  := true
            dir := nHi >= nLo ? -1 : 1
            who := f_who(divP, divY, okN, okE, int(n.d2), int(e.d2))

    // ── PCP: the bar that just closed, [1]. A PCP is only a disagreement of
    //    direction, so it needs no swing and no confirming bar — it is known
    //    one bar earlier than the PSP that may or may not follow it.
    qN = i_use_nq and not na(n.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or n.d1 != 0)
    qE = i_use_es and not na(e.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or e.d1 != 0)
    qY = i_use_ym and not na(y.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or y.d1 != 0)

    qP  = qN and qE and n.d1 != e.d1
    qYm = qY and y.d1 > 0 and ((qE and e.d1 < 0) or (qN and n.d1 < 0))

    pOn  = qP or qYm
    pWho = pOn ? f_who(qP, qYm, qN, qE, int(n.d1), int(e.d1)) : ""
    [on, dir, who, pOn, pWho]

[on15, dir15, who15, pcp15, pwho15] = f_flash(n15, e15, y15)
[on5m, dir5m, who5m, pcp5m, pwho5m] = f_flash(n5m, e5m, y5m)

// Kept as one-line statements on purpose: Pine treats a continuation line
// indented by any multiple of four spaces as the start of a block, so a
// column-aligned wrapped ternary is a syntax error waiting to happen.
mtfTop = i_mtf_h == "שמאל" ? position.top_left : i_mtf_h == "מרכז" ? position.top_center : position.top_right
mtfMid = i_mtf_h == "שמאל" ? position.middle_left : i_mtf_h == "מרכז" ? position.middle_center : position.middle_right
mtfBot = i_mtf_h == "שמאל" ? position.bottom_left : i_mtf_h == "מרכז" ? position.bottom_center : position.bottom_right
mtfPos = i_mtf_v == "למעלה" ? mtfTop : i_mtf_v == "באמצע" ? mtfMid : mtfBot

// Padding: the table is anchored to an edge, so empty spacer rows on the edge
// side push the content away from it. Anchored at the top the spacers go
// above the content, otherwise below it.
mtfUp  = i_mtf_v == "למעלה"
mtfRow = mtfUp ? i_mtf_pad : 0

// One cell per timeframe, not one joined string: a cell carries a single
// text colour, and each timeframe has to be painted in its own state's.
var table mtfTbl = table.new(mtfPos, 7, 1 + i_mtf_pad, border_width = 0)

c_clear = color.new(color.black, 100)

if barstate.islast and i_mtf_on
    if i_mtf_pad > 0
        for k = 0 to i_mtf_pad - 1
            table.cell(mtfTbl, 0, mtfUp ? k : 1 + k, " ",
                 text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)

    anything = r1w != "" or r1d != "" or r4h != "" or r1h != "" or rCh != ""
    table.cell(mtfTbl, 0, mtfRow, anything ? "ADI" : "", text_color = i_col_neut,
         text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)

    col = 1
    if r1w != ""
        table.cell(mtfTbl, col, mtfRow, r1w, text_color = f_col(st1w),
             text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        col := col + 1
    if r1d != ""
        table.cell(mtfTbl, col, mtfRow, r1d, text_color = f_col(st1d),
             text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        col := col + 1
    if r4h != ""
        table.cell(mtfTbl, col, mtfRow, r4h, text_color = f_col(st4h),
             text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        col := col + 1
    if r1h != ""
        table.cell(mtfTbl, col, mtfRow, r1h, text_color = f_col(st1h),
             text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        col := col + 1
    if rCh != ""
        table.cell(mtfTbl, col, mtfRow, rCh, text_color = f_col(stCh),
             text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        col := col + 1
    if col <= 6
        for k = col to 6
            table.cell(mtfTbl, k, mtfRow, "", bgcolor = c_clear)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE FAST NOTICE  —  5m / 15m, in a box of its own
//
//  Deliberately NOT the carried-state engine, and deliberately not part of the
//  breaks line. A PSP is a function of three bars and a PCP of one, so both
//  can be read straight off the last bar with nothing accumulated across
//  history — which is what lets this report a timeframe BELOW the chart's,
//  where sampling once per chart bar would corrupt any carried state.
//
//  No timer is needed, and none is possible to get wrong: the request always
//  reports the state as of the last CLOSED bar of that timeframe, so the
//  notice is replaced wholesale at the next close of ITS OWN timeframe —
//  which is exactly "stands for about five minutes, then goes".
//
//  Each timeframe is skipped on its own chart, where the bars already carry
//  the marker: no 5m notice on a 5m chart, no 15m notice on a 15m chart.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

ok15 = i_fast_on and chartSec != 900
ok5m = i_fast_on and chartSec != 300

psp15 = ok15 and on15
psp5m = ok5m and on5m
pnd15 = ok15 and i_fast_pcp and pcp15 and not on15
pnd5m = ok5m and i_fast_pcp and pcp5m and not on5m

f15 = psp15 ? "⚡ PSP 15m " + (dir15 < 0 ? "▼" : "▲") + " " + who15 : pnd15 ? "◦ PCP 15m " + pwho15 : ""
f5m = psp5m ? "⚡ PSP 5m " + (dir5m < 0 ? "▼" : "▲") + " " + who5m : pnd5m ? "◦ PCP 5m " + pwho5m : ""

fc15 = psp15 ? (dir15 < 0 ? i_col_bear : i_col_bull) : i_col_pend
fc5m = psp5m ? (dir5m < 0 ? i_col_bear : i_col_bull) : i_col_pend

// The tint is what makes it read as a notice instead of a label. Only a PSP
// gets one; a PCP stays flat grey so the two can never be confused.
fb15 = i_fast_bg and psp15 ? color.new(dir15 < 0 ? i_col_bear : i_col_bull, 82) : c_clear
fb5m = i_fast_bg and psp5m ? color.new(dir5m < 0 ? i_col_bear : i_col_bull, 82) : c_clear

// One-line statements on purpose — see the note above mtfTop.
fastTop = i_fast_h == "שמאל" ? position.top_left : i_fast_h == "מרכז" ? position.top_center : position.top_right
fastMid = i_fast_h == "שמאל" ? position.middle_left : i_fast_h == "מרכז" ? position.middle_center : position.middle_right
fastBot = i_fast_h == "שמאל" ? position.bottom_left : i_fast_h == "מרכז" ? position.bottom_center : position.bottom_right
fastPos = i_fast_v == "למעלה" ? fastTop : i_fast_v == "באמצע" ? fastMid : fastBot
fastSz  = i_fast_sz == "קטן" ? size.small : i_fast_sz == "רגיל" ? size.normal : i_fast_sz == "ענק" ? size.huge : size.large

fastUp = i_fast_v == "למעלה"
fastR0 = fastUp ? i_fast_pad : 0

var table fastTbl = table.new(fastPos, 1, 2 + i_fast_pad, border_width = 0)

if barstate.islast and i_fast_on
    if i_fast_pad > 0
        for k = 0 to i_fast_pad - 1
            table.cell(fastTbl, 0, fastUp ? k : 2 + k, " ",
                 text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)

    table.cell(fastTbl, 0, fastR0, f15, text_color = fc15,
         text_size = fastSz, bgcolor = fb15)
    table.cell(fastTbl, 0, fastR0 + 1, f5m, text_color = fc5m,
         text_size = fastSz, bgcolor = fb5m)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PANEL  (optional, off by default)
//  The full picture: every timeframe's live break, or its grey pending bar.
//  The line shows only the most recent, so the two complement each other.
//  "▶" marks a timeframe at or below the chart's — drawn on the bars instead.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

pnlTop = i_pnl_h == "שמאל" ? position.top_left : i_pnl_h == "מרכז" ? position.top_center : position.top_right
pnlMid = i_pnl_h == "שמאל" ? position.middle_left : i_pnl_h == "מרכז" ? position.middle_center : position.middle_right
pnlBot = i_pnl_h == "שמאל" ? position.bottom_left : i_pnl_h == "מרכז" ? position.bottom_center : position.bottom_right
pnlPos = i_pnl_v == "למעלה" ? pnlTop : i_pnl_v == "באמצע" ? pnlMid : pnlBot

pnlUp  = i_pnl_v == "למעלה"
pnlR0  = pnlUp ? i_pnl_pad : 0

dbgRows = i_debug ? 4 : 0   // NQ, ES, YM, d1

var table pnlTbl = table.new(pnlPos, 2, 6 + dbgRows + i_pnl_pad, border_width = 0)

// The raw values the chart-timeframe engine is working from. d1 is the bar
// that just closed, d2 the one before it — the swing candidate.
f_d(float d) =>
    na(d) ? "na" : d > 0 ? "+1" : d < 0 ? "-1" : "0"

f_row3(float n, float e, float y) =>
    "N" + f_d(n) + " E" + f_d(e) + " Y" + f_d(y)

f_flag(bool b) =>
    b ? "1" : "0"

// The open and close actually read for the last closed bar, to be compared
// against the same candle on the chart.
f_oc(float o, float c) =>
    "o" + str.tostring(o, "#.##") + " c" + str.tostring(c, "#.##")

f_stat(MtfSt s, bool shown) =>
    not shown ? "▶" : s.live ? f_arrow(s) + " " + s.who : s.pndOn ? "◦ " + s.pndWho : "—"

f_statCol(MtfSt s, bool shown) =>
    not shown or not s.live ? i_col_neut : s.dir < 0 ? i_col_bear : i_col_bull

if barstate.islast and i_pnl_on
    if i_pnl_pad > 0
        for k = 0 to i_pnl_pad - 1
            table.cell(pnlTbl, 0, pnlUp ? k : 6 + dbgRows + k, " ",
                 text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)

    table.cell(pnlTbl, 0, pnlR0, "ADI", text_color = i_col_neut, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
    table.cell(pnlTbl, 1, pnlR0, "",    text_color = i_col_neut, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
    table.cell(pnlTbl, 0, pnlR0 + 1, "1W", text_color = f_statCol(st1w, sh1w), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
    table.cell(pnlTbl, 1, pnlR0 + 1, f_stat(st1w, sh1w), text_color = f_statCol(st1w, sh1w), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
    table.cell(pnlTbl, 0, pnlR0 + 2, "1D", text_color = f_statCol(st1d, sh1d), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
    table.cell(pnlTbl, 1, pnlR0 + 2, f_stat(st1d, sh1d), text_color = f_statCol(st1d, sh1d), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
    table.cell(pnlTbl, 0, pnlR0 + 3, "4H", text_color = f_statCol(st4h, sh4h), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
    table.cell(pnlTbl, 1, pnlR0 + 3, f_stat(st4h, sh4h), text_color = f_statCol(st4h, sh4h), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
    table.cell(pnlTbl, 0, pnlR0 + 4, "1H", text_color = f_statCol(st1h, sh1h), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
    table.cell(pnlTbl, 1, pnlR0 + 4, f_stat(st1h, sh1h), text_color = f_statCol(st1h, sh1h), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
    table.cell(pnlTbl, 0, pnlR0 + 5, chName, text_color = f_statCol(stCh, tf_allowed), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
    table.cell(pnlTbl, 1, pnlR0 + 5, f_stat(stCh, tf_allowed), text_color = f_statCol(stCh, tf_allowed), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)

    if i_debug
        table.cell(pnlTbl, 0, pnlR0 + 6, "NQ", text_color = i_col_neut, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        table.cell(pnlTbl, 1, pnlR0 + 6, f_oc(a_nq_o[1], a_nq_c[1]), text_color = i_col_neut, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        table.cell(pnlTbl, 0, pnlR0 + 7, "ES", text_color = i_col_neut, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        table.cell(pnlTbl, 1, pnlR0 + 7, f_oc(a_es_o[1], a_es_c[1]), text_color = i_col_neut, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        table.cell(pnlTbl, 0, pnlR0 + 8, "YM", text_color = i_col_neut, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        table.cell(pnlTbl, 1, pnlR0 + 8, f_oc(a_ym_o[1], a_ym_c[1]), text_color = i_col_neut, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        table.cell(pnlTbl, 0, pnlR0 + 9, "d1", text_color = i_col_neut, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)
        table.cell(pnlTbl, 1, pnlR0 + 9, f_row3(nCh.d1, eCh.d1, yCh.d1) + "  pnd" + f_flag(stCh.pndOn), text_color = i_col_neut, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  ALERTS
//  Two events, two messages, so a phone notification says which happened.
//  The grey pending state deliberately raises nothing — it is a heads-up on
//  the chart, not something worth waking you for.
//  Alerts run on TradingView's servers, so one alert on one chart keeps
//  working with the chart closed.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// dir and who outlive an invalidation, so a broken break can still name
// itself here.
f_alertTx(MtfSt s, string nm) =>
    nm + " " + f_arrow(s) + " " + s.who

newTx  = sh1w and st1w.isNew ? f_alertTx(st1w, "1W") : sh1d and st1d.isNew ? f_alertTx(st1d, "1D") : sh4h and st4h.isNew ? f_alertTx(st4h, "4H") : sh1h and st1h.isNew ? f_alertTx(st1h, "1H") : tf_allowed and stCh.isNew ? f_alertTx(stCh, chName) : ""
goneTx = sh1w and st1w.isGone ? f_alertTx(st1w, "1W") : sh1d and st1d.isGone ? f_alertTx(st1d, "1D") : sh4h and st4h.isGone ? f_alertTx(st4h, "4H") : sh1h and st1h.isGone ? f_alertTx(st1h, "1H") : tf_allowed and stCh.isGone ? f_alertTx(stCh, chName) : ""

if i_mtf_alert and i_mtf_on and goneTx != ""
    alert("ADI: נשבר — " + goneTx, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

if i_mtf_alert and i_mtf_on and newTx != ""
    alert("ADI: " + newTx, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// The fast notice, as a real alert TradingView can push. Once per CHART bar at
// most — on an hourly chart that is once an hour, so a second fast PSP inside
// the same hour shows in the box but does not ring twice.
// Seeded from a series expression, not from "", so the variable is series
// string from the start and the append below has something it can assign to.
fastTx = psp5m ? "5m " + (dir5m < 0 ? "▼" : "▲") + " " + who5m : ""
if psp15
    fastTx := fastTx + (fastTx == "" ? "" : "  ·  ") + "15m " + (dir15 < 0 ? "▼" : "▲") + " " + who15

if i_fast_on and i_fast_alert and fastTx != ""
    alert("ADI מהיר — PSP " + fastTx, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  END OF SCRIPT
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
